  "policy_quote": "For a delivered order, each item can be exchanged to an available new item of the **same product** but of different product option. There cannot be any change of product types, e.g. modify shirt to shoe. The user must provide a payment method to pay or receive refund of the price difference. If the user provides a gift card, it must have enough balance to cover the price difference.",

  "evidence_quote": "→ TOOL_CALL exchange_delivered_order_items: {\"order_id\": \"#W3470184\", \"item_ids\": [\"2757705742\"], \"new_item_ids\": [\"8555936349\"], \"payment_method_id\": \"gift_card_7245904\"}",

  "analysis": "The policy requires that exchanged items must be of the **same product** (Wireless Earbuds) but allow different product options (e.g., IPX7 vs. IPX4). The evidence shows the exchange is between **item 2757705742 (IPX7)** and **item 8555936349 (IPX4)**, both under the same product (Wireless Earbuds). However, the **gift card balance ($17.00) is insufficient** to cover the refund of **$32.48**, violating the policy requirement that the gift card must have enough balance to cover the price difference. The claim about the item not being the cheapest is unrelated to the policy violation being evaluated here (payment method balance).",

  "verdict": "REFUTED"
}
